# README Adoption SoT

[`README.md`](../../README.md) is the **adoption / first-run SoT**: problem/solution, quick start, commands at a glance, essential flags, short config, output formats + exit codes, short programmatic API, documentation hub, limitations, and pointers to CONTRIBUTING / SECURITY / License.

It is **not** a CLI flag encyclopedia, pipeline internals guide, progress/TTY cookbook, or milestone tracker.

## Ownership matrix

| Change type | Destination |
| ----------- | ----------- |
| Adoption pitch, essential flags, exit codes, short API | **README.md** |
| Flag encyclopedia, pipeline internals, progress/TTY, assess/explain long | **`docs/cli-reference.md`** |
| Cookbooks / workflows | **`docs/recipes.md`** |
| Why NCLOC / indentation | **`docs/methodology.md`** |
| Warning code catalog | **`docs/warning-codes.md`** |
| Exit-code policy for agents | **AGENTS.md** |
| Milestone status, feature history | **ROADMAP.md** / `.specs/features/` |
| Decisions, deferred ideas, blockers | **STATE.md** |

## Forbidden in README.md

- `## Advanced`, `## Features` marketing dumps
- Encyclopedia headings: Pipeline detail, Performance and diagnostics, Rename confidence, Command synopsis and flags
- Full flag laundry lists (keep essential flags only; full list → cli-reference / `--help`)
- Milestone tags: `\bM\d+\b` (e.g. `M71`)
- Changelog voice: “shipped in M…”, Execute ownership by milestone number

## Allowed

- Problem / solution / zero-network callout
- Quick start, commands table, use-this-when, how-it-works (short) + methodology link
- Essential flags (~8), requirements, shell completion install one-liners
- Configuration summary + recipes/monorepo links
- Output formats overview + exit-code table; short Programmatic API sample
- Documentation hub linking recipes, methodology, warning-codes, cli-reference

## Sync rule

When living docs change after Execute:

1. New **essential** user-facing flag → one row in README Essential flags **and** full entry in `docs/cli-reference.md`.
2. Power-user / internals / progress / assess detail → **`docs/cli-reference.md` only** (optional one-line README pointer).
3. Workflows / copy-paste → **`docs/recipes.md`**.
4. Self-check: *Would a first-time adopter need this on the first screen?* If no → wrong file (cli-reference or recipes).

Editorial lint: [living-sot-doc.mjs](../hooks/lib/living-sot-doc.mjs) `lintReadmeDoc` (hooks + `pnpm hooks:smoke`).
